      "questions": [
        {
          "id": "q1_1",
          "type": "mcq",
          "text": "<p>Let x be an integer which can take a value of 0 or 1. The statement if (x == 0)x = 1; else x = 0;\n                        is equivalent to which one of the following?</p>",
          "options": [
            "x = 1 - x",
            "x = x + 1",
            "x = x * 1",
            "x = 1% x"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "q1_2",
          "type": "mcq",
          "text": "<p>A program attempts to generate as many permutations as possible of the string, 'abcd' by pushing\n                        the characters a, b, c, d in the same order onto a stack, but it may pop off the top character\n                        at any time. Which one of the following strings cannot be generated using this program?</p>",
          "options": [
            "abcd",
            "dcba",
            "cabd",
            "cbad"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "q1_3",
          "type": "mcq",
          "text": "<p>Suppose a C program has floating constant 1.414, what is the best way to convert this 'float'\n                        data type?</p>",
          "options": [
            "(float)1.414",
            "Float (1.414)",
            "1.414f or 1.414F",
            "1.414 itself of 'float' data type, i.e., nothing else required"
          ]
        },
        {
